microscope-views 1

# Node's library types, of the classes it writes in JavaScript. Verified
# against Node 22, 24, and 26 by tests/node/views.rs. A class is named by
# the script that defines its constructor: node:buffer's Buffer is
# node::buffer::Buffer, and V8's own classes, which no script defines, by
# their names alone.

# Every typed array draws its elements as a line, read at once. A Buffer is
# one too: its prototype's constructor is Buffer, whose own prototype's is
# Uint8Array.
view javascript TypedArray {
    visualize "line-plot"
}

# An emitter's listeners, by event name: one function, or an array of them
# in the order they run. Node keeps them in `_events`, which an emitter
# whose constructor never ran inherits as undefined. Its limit on listeners
# is left out: an emitter without its own has Node's default, which only a
# getter reads.
view javascript node::events::EventEmitter {
    field listeners = self._events
}
